messages:
mike: Quick ask — debugging a customer tokenization failure (support #1234). I need to capture one request+response sample from staging that contains a phone number in the request body so we can repro. Can we do a 1-hour ephemeral capture with redaction/pseudonymization?

olivia: Don't capture raw PII. We need one of: redact (replace with <REDACTED>), store only last4, or HMAC with a team key. HMAC is preferred if you need to correlate requests across systems. Also we must strip Authorization-like headers and not log full prompt text.

mike: HMAC sounds good. What's the minimal implementation? I can add a small middleware in the staging proxy.

olivia: Use HMAC-SHA256 with a KMS-managed key and a short TTL. Example pseudocode we use for similar captures:
```
// pseudocode middleware
const phone = body.phone_number;
const hmac = HMAC_SHA256(kms.getKey('team-debug'), phone);
body.phone_number = `hmac:${hmac}`;
// also remove full prompt fields and any tokens from headers
delete headers['authorization'];
delete headers['x-api-token'];
```
Make sure the plaintext never touches logs or S3. Store the captured artifacts in the restricted debug S3 bucket with encryption and a 1-hour auto-delete lifecycle.

mike: Ok I'll implement that. Two questions: (1) Do we need an approval from Sec? (2) Who should be able to request access if we need to review plaintext later?

olivia: (1) Yes, we need an explicit approval in thread for the TTL and scope. (2) Access to plaintext must be via a documented break-glass flow: short lived KMS unwrap + logged approval by a security approver (role: eng-security). We prefer to avoid providing any path to view plaintext unless absolutely necessary.

samir: For the approval: +1 for HMAC + 1-hour TTL in staging. Please ensure that the KMS key is not copyable and has conditional IAM.

anya: Quick nit: mask the log samples too. Any prompt snippets in the payload must be redacted to first 20 characters only, then <TRUNC>. Example: `prompt = prompt.slice(0,20) + '<TRUNC>'`.

security-bot: Policy note — temporary captures with PII must be logged in the capture registry: /infra/debug-captures.csv and include requester, reason, start_ts, expiry_ts. Approvals are required before capture starts.

mike: Thanks all — implementing HMAC middleware + S3 retention + capture-registry entry. Posting the PR shortly and will tag @olivia for final sign-off. :thumbsup:

olivia: Sounds good — ping when PR is up and include the pseudo-code and KMS key ARN. I can sign off after a quick review. :white_check_mark:
